<main>
  <section class="hero-donnees">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h1>Data & Decision-Making</h1>
      <p>National center for biological data collection and analysis supporting conservation and public health.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="page-section">
    <div class="wrap">
      
      <div class="intro-text">
        <p>
          <strong>Data is our primary tool.</strong> Before planting, treating, or designing landscapes, we must understand.  
          The Jardin Botanique des Cayes transforms raw field observations into structured databases.  
          These data enable government agencies and researchers to make evidence-based decisions for ecosystem survival and public health security.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="data-module">
        <div class="module-img">
          <img src="{{ 'images/donnees/donnees-biodiversite-ecosystemes.jpg' | relative_url }}" alt="Forest Inventory">
          <div class="img-caption">Floristic Inventory & Taxonomy</div>
        </div>
        <div class="module-content">
          <h2><i class="fa-solid fa-tree"></i> Biodiversity & Ecosystems</h2>
          <div class="module-desc">
            We conduct comprehensive inventories of the flora of Haiti’s Grand Sud region. Each plant is identified, geolocated, and classified according to international standards (APG IV) to guide restoration and reforestation efforts.
          </div>
          <ul class="data-list">
            <li class="data-item">
              <span class="data-label">Taxonomy</span>
              <span class="data-val">Accurate botanical identification, updated family and genus classifications, and management of the National Herbarium.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="data-item">
              <span class="data-label">IUCN Status</span>
              <span class="data-val">Assessment of threatened species (CR, EN, VU) to prioritize urgent conservation actions.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="data-item">
              <span class="data-label">Mapping</span>
              <span class="data-val">Delineation of Key Biodiversity Areas (KBAs) and monitoring of critical habitats (mangroves, dry forests).</span>
            </li>
            <li class="data-item">
              <span class="data-label">Invasive Species</span>
              <span class="data-val">Monitoring the spread of exotic species threatening agriculture and native flora.</span>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="data-module reverse">
        <div class="module-img">
          <img src="{{ 'images/donnees/donnees-pharmacognosie.png' | relative_url }}" alt="Medicinal Plant Preparation">
          <div class="img-caption">Ethnobotany & Pharmacognosy</div>
        </div>
        <div class="module-content">
          <h2><i class="fa-solid fa-heart-pulse"></i> Human Health & Phytotherapy</h2>
          <div class="module-desc">
            A majority of Haitians rely on medicinal plants for healthcare. Our mission is to ensure safety and scientific validation of traditional practices while identifying toxicity risks.
          </div>
          <ul class="data-list">
            <li class="data-item">
              <span class="data-label">Ethnobotany</span>
              <span class="data-val">Documentation of local knowledge: which plants are used, for which conditions, and at what dosages.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="data-item">
              <span class="data-label">Toxicology</span>
              <span class="data-val"><strong>Critical data:</strong> Identification of toxic plants frequently mistaken for remedies to prevent fatal poisonings.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="data-item">
              <span class="data-label">Phytochemistry</span>
              <span class="data-val">Analysis of active compounds to validate the real efficacy of traditional treatments.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="data-item">
              <span class="data-label">Nutrition</span>
              <span class="data-val">Promotion of non-conventional food plants (NUS) to combat malnutrition.</span>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="data-module">
        <div class="module-img">
          <img src="{{ 'images/donnees/donnees-modelisation-climatique.jpg' | relative_url }}" alt="Landscape Modeling">
          <div class="img-caption">Modeling & Resilience</div>
        </div>
        <div class="module-content">
          <h2><i class="fa-solid fa-chart-line"></i> Climate & Territory</h2>
          <div class="module-desc">
            In the face of climate change, random planting is no longer an option. We use ecological modeling to anticipate Haiti’s environmental future and propose sustainable solutions.
          </div>
          <ul class="data-list">
            <li class="data-item">
              <span class="data-label">Modeling</span>
              <span class="data-val">Projection of future ecological niches: which species will survive in 10, 20, or 50 years?</span>
            </li>
            <li class="data-item">
              <span class="data-label">Resilience</span>
              <span class="data-val">Identification of species resistant to cyclones and prolonged drought.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="data-item">
              <span class="data-label">Soil & Water</span>
              <span class="data-val">Selection of plants for soil stabilization (erosion control) and watershed protection.</span>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>

